# Goal

A follow-up review round can be limited to chosen paths: `next --only P` (repeatable) computes the scale, the commit list, the changed files and the read commands of `scope.md` over those pathspecs only, states the limit in the scope, and refuses to create a round when any one pathspec, or the combined set, selects no change. Without `--only`, `next` and `summary` are unchanged.

Correct only if:
- every git fact in the generated scope takes the same pathspec list;
- a dead pathspec is an error before `revmux new`, never a silently empty scope;
- `--only` and `--exclude` stay separate (`--exclude` remains prose for reviewers);
- the tests would fail if any of these regressed;
- `SKILL.md` describes the option the way the script behaves.

Finding nothing is a valid answer.
